ency predictor in the clean stratum; the signed estimate is negative, i.e. opposite the pre-registered direction. H56 rejects ERBB2 amplification as a meaningful stronger-dependency predictor in the same stratum. H57 gives no clear support for research_signature_a >= 1 enhancing the SMARCA4-loss effect; the interaction is essentially null (+0.014), but the CI still reaches slightly above threshold, so I keep it unresolved/deferred rather than claiming absence of interaction. I request independent validation for H13, the KEAP1-loss main effect, because it is an accepted post-hoc reversal with very large precise discovery evidence but no independent validation; validating this protects against a post-hoc reversal or co-occurrence artifact. All claims remain associations in the supplied dataset, not causal or generalizable claims.",
