ct; subthreshold or opposite estimates should make the broader claim context-sensitive. Residual clean-marker claims with threshold-level point estimate and interval above 0.15 become validation candidates; borderline intervals remain unresolved. For SMARCA4 robustness, robust non-Avana/squamous/MSI context would make H43 safer for independent validation and broader dataset-level interpretation. Null/subthreshold non-Avana or squamous results would argue against claiming generalization across library or lineage. For PTEN, robust conditional effects would support independence from TP53/SMARCA4 axes; attenuation would be scientifically useful but not reverse main PTEN.\n\nDeferred/lower priority: H16-H18 lineage-specific accepted marker checks; H23 PTEN in PIK3CA-wildtype; H44 SMARCA4-by-lineage interaction because direct squamous test now added; H29/H30 TP53/MSI interactions due small MSI-positive overlap cells; CDKN2A H42/H54 borderline unresolved; research_signature_a interaction H57; other rejected markers unless a new specific hypothesis arises. Validation budget after prior validations: 7 new voluntary validations remaining. Next validation priority after appraise: H43 broad SMARCA4 main if context checks support robustness; alternative candidates H10 MSI_high main and H11 TP53_loss main. Keep all claims as dataset-level associations and do not infer causality or external generalizability."
