{
  "narrative": "I interpret signed estimates consistently: for direction -1 claims, positive signed estimates indicate stronger measured dependency in the exposed group, i.e. a more negative raw dependency_composite; for direction +1 claims, positive signed estimates indicate a higher/less-negative raw composite and therefore weaker measured dependency. The new results refine the context structure of the central dataset associations. H18 and H83 test MSI-high within adenocarcinoma and squamous subgroups, respectively. Both remain strong and threshold-level: H18 gives +0.740 (CI +0.611 to +0.869) and H83 gives +0.862 (CI +0.644 to +1.080). These are decisive evidence that the overall MSI-high stronger-dependency association is not confined to one histology, so I accept and close them as histologic robustness tests. The formal lineage interaction H86 is not supported in its claimed direction: signed estimate -0.122, CI -0.373 to +0.129. The upper bound is below +0.15, so the registered claimed direction is excluded; this does not establish absence of any opposite effect, but the point estimate is also not threshold-level, so no new reverse interaction claim is warranted. I therefore reject and close H86 as a context-modification claim, leaving the main MSI association H10 unchanged and now preparing validation.\n\nThe central-marker interaction tests are mostly reassuring but not uniformly decisive. H87, TP53 loss by SMARCA4-loss context, is +0.070 with CI -0.053 to +0.192. It is not threshold-level at the point estimate, but its interval overlaps meaningful positive values, so it remains unresolved and deferred. H88, KEAP1 loss by SMARCA4-loss context, is -0.018 with CI -0.161 to +0.124; the claimed positive direction is excluded by the upper bound below threshold, so I reject and close this registered claim. H89, PTEN loss by KEAP1-loss context, is -0.114 with CI -0.322 to +0.093; again the claimed positive direction is excluded, although an opposite effect is not established because the point estimate is below threshold. I reject and close the registered direction. H90, CDKN2A loss by SMARCA4-loss context, is -0.065 with CI -0.227 to +0.098; the claimed positive direction is excluded and the observed effect is not threshold-level, so I reject and close this registered CDKN2A context claim. CDKN2A itself remains borderline in main and stratified mean-difference tests, but these interaction results do not establish a robust SMARCA4-context modification. H84 and H85 remain unresolved deferred: H84, PTEN by lineage, is -0.041 with CI -0.260 to +0.178, and H85, CDKN2A by TP53 loss, is +0.063 with CI -0.098 to +0.224. These intervals overlap meaningful values in at least one direction, so I do not convert them into accepted context claims; they are low priority because the main PTEN effect is independently validated and CDKN2A remains non-threshold overall.\n\nThe residual clean-stratum marker tests are close to null and can be closed. H58 APC mutation in the cleaner stratum is -0.037 (CI -0.083 to +0.010), H59 NF1 loss is +0.002 (CI -0.067 to +0.070), and H71 SMAD4 loss is -0.034 (CI -0.099 to +0.030). Their intervals are near zero and do not support threshold-level effects in the registered directions. I reject and close all three. Taken together, these 12 analyses support approximate context independence among the dominant dataset-level marker axes, while not adding any new high-value unvalidated main association. The most informative next validation is still H10, the overall MSI-high main effect: it has a large discovery effect, strong conditional robustness including histology, TP53-loss, KEAP1-loss, SMARCA4-loss, and cleaner-background tests, but it has not yet received independent validation. I therefore request validation of H10. Multiplicity and small-cell uncertainty remain relevant, especially for histologic MSI-high tests, but the accepted new subgroup results are far above threshold, whereas borderline CDKN2A and several interaction results remain unresolved or closed for the registered direction only. All conclusions remain associations in the supplied dataset, not causal mechanisms or externally generalizable claims.",
