  "narrative": "Signed convention: for direction -1 claims, a positive signed estimate means the exposed group has a lower raw dependency_composite and therefore stronger measured dependency; for direction +1 claims, a positive signed estimate means a higher raw composite and therefore weaker measured dependency. The scientifically meaningful threshold is 0.15 composite dependency-score units in the claimed direction. I propose three focused follow-ups that use a measured biological expression assay rather than a constructed research assay: elevated rnaseq_AXL_log2_tpm contexts for KEAP1 loss, MSI-high, and PTEN loss. The existing active H113-H119 tests MYC-high and AXL-high contexts for TP53 loss, SMARCA4 loss, PTEN loss in MYC, MSI-high in MYC, and TP53/SMARCA4 in AXL. These three proposals complete a more balanced set of AXL-high context-robustness checks for the central marker axes. The KEAP1-loss hypothesis is that the strong weak-dependency association, i.e. higher raw composite in KEAP1-loss samples, persists in AXL-high samples; registered direction is +1 and alternatives are null, attenuated, or reverse. The MSI-high hypothesis is that the strong stronger-dependency association, i.e. lower raw composite in MSI-high samples, persists in moderate-high AXL; registered direction is -1 and alternatives are null, attenuated, or reverse. I use AXL >=3.5 for MSI-high rather than >=4.0 to retain adequate exposed cell counts. The PTEN-loss hypothesis is that the moderate stronger-dependency association persists in moderate-high AXL; registered direction is -1. PTEN is scientifically the most useful of the three because its context map is less uniform than for TP53 loss, SMARCA4 loss, KEAP1 loss, or MSI-high: a threshold-level result would strengthen PTEN context robustness, whereas an attenuated or null result would further identify a boundary condition for the main PTEN association. I also defer H122, media_serum 5 versus 2, as an investigation-only change. It is status unresolved but low priority relative to marker-context and remaining technical residual questions because the broader media-serum contrasts have been null or subthreshold in registered directions. These new comparisons remain dataset-level associations only and do not establish causality, mechanism, or external generalizability.",
