  "narrative": "Iteration 14 synthesis and final scientific report. Signed convention: for direction -1, a positive signed estimate means exposed minus comparator has stronger measured dependency (more negative dependency_composite); for direction +1, a positive signed estimate means weaker measured dependency. The effect-size threshold is 0.15 composite dependency-score units in the claimed direction. Due validation assessment: H158 tested CDKN2A loss in high aneuploidy cells with direction -1 (stronger dependency). Discovery estimate R149 is +0.283 (95% Welch interval +0.118 to +0.449), which is direction-consistent and near threshold, but the independent validation estimate R156 is only +0.048 with a conservative interval -0.184 to +0.280. The validation point estimate is below threshold and does not exclude zero, so the combined discovery-and-validation evidence does not support the registered claim. H158 is therefore rejected and closed. This is a failure to support CDKN2A in this context, not proof that CDKN2A has no effect in any context. Together with the validated-negative high-MYC context H127 and the validated-negative core-negative high-aneuploidy context H165, CDKN2A loss now has no robust dataset-level threshold support in this supplied dataset. Supported dataset-level findings. SMARCA4 loss is the strongest stronger-dependency association: main signed estimate +0.804 (95% interval +0.742 to +0.867) and independent validation +0.803 (+0.712 to +0.894). It remains strong in high-aneuploidy cells (+0.779, +0.636 to +0.922) and in several expression, marker, and copy-number-robust contexts; the formal SMARCA4-by-high-aneuploidy interaction H183 was rejected. MSI-high status is also strongly associated with stronger measured dependency: main signed estimate +0.775 (+0.664 to +0.885) and validation +0.831 (+0.668 to +0.993), with accepted subgroup and context checks but no established effect-modification contrasts. TP53 loss is strongly associated with weaker measured dependency (direction +1): main signed estimate +0.829 (+0.767 to +0.891) and validation +0.771 (+0.673 to +0.868). KEAP1 loss is also strongly associated with weaker measured dependency: main signed estimate +0.810 (+0.745 to +0.875) and validation +0.840 (+0.754 to +0.926). These core effects are robust across high-aneuploidy, MYC/AXL-expression, hypoxia, EMT, research-signature, marker-background, and library subsets. Formal interactions for these markers are mostly rejected or remain unresolved but are not needed for the main-effect conclusions. PTEN loss is a moderately and broadly supported stronger-dependency association: main discovery +0.239 (+0.145 to +0.332) and independent validation +0.294 (+0.149 to +0.439). Context-specific accepted support includes TP53-negative, KEAP1-negative, Avana-library, high-MYC, high-aneuploidy main-effect, high-Cas9, and lower-Cas9 settings. However, context dependence is not established: PTEN-by-high-aneuploidy interaction remains unresolved and closed, PTEN-by-high-AXL interaction was rejected, and several high-AXL or mutation-burden PTEN boundary estimates remain imprecise. Negative or unsupported comparisons include lineage subtype, KRAS mutation, EGFR amplification, BRAF V600E, MTAP loss, STK11 loss, MYC amplification, research markers D/E/F, sex, media-serum contrasts, screen batch, CRISPR-library and omics-availability contrasts, and most tested interactions. These are non-findings in this dataset under the stated threshold and uncertainty criteria. Unresolved uncertainty is concentrated in PTEN context boundaries and residual CDKN2A conditional signals. For PTEN, the broad signal is supported, but high-AXL and other subgroup estimates are near threshold with intervals spanning zero or lower bounds below threshold; the appropriate summary is a broad moderate association without confirmed context modification. For CDKN2A, multiple discovery-only contexts have positive point estimates around or above threshold, but the most plausible validated contexts failed. I closed the remaining active CDKN2A context H143 as a low-priority non-robust line; that is a prioritization decision, not an empirical rejection of that exact comparison. Most informative next analysis, if discovery-only work continues, is to run the already active robustness checks for the supported core effects: PTEN in high-stemness, high-EMT, and high-hypoxia contexts (H141, H145, H147), plus core-marker high-stemness checks H151-H153 and KEAP1 high-EMT H146. The active PTEN core-negative high-aneuploidy comparison H177 is scientifically informative but may be cell-count limited; if analyzed, interpret it as a cautiously qualified main-effect check, not an interaction test, and do not overstate it if below threshold or invalid. Further CDKN2A tests should generally wait unless a new, well-powered context with a credible validation path exists. Since no validation requests remain, any future results can refine discovery-level descriptions but cannot independently validate new claims in this run. All conclusions are dataset-level associations in the supplied 2000-line lung dataset. They do not establish causality, a single-gene knockout mechanism, biological meaning of constructed research assays, or external generalizability.",
  "research_notes": "Iteration 14 synthesis update. Signed convention retained: direction -1 positive = stronger dependency; direction +1 positive = weaker dependency; threshold 0.15 units. H158 (CDKN2A high aneuploidy) reassessed due validation deadline: discovery +0.283 (0.118 to 0.449), independent validation +0.048 (-0.184 to 0.280). Rejected and closed; CDKN2A remains non-robust after H127 and H165 validation failures. H143 active CDKN2A stemness closed as low-priority without empirical rejection. Remaining active priorities are PTEN core-context robustness H141/H145/H147, core-marker stemness H151-H153, KEAP1 EMT H146, and cautiously PTEN core-negative high-aneuploidy H177. No validation requests remain. Conclusions are dataset-level associations only, not causal or generalizable."
