ement. The plausible alternative is that PTEN loss is not modified by screen quality and any apparent elevation reflects imprecision or confounding. For the core-negative PTEN interactions, the earlier high-Wnt all-population interaction R207 was suggestive but imprecise, and the core-negative high-AXL simple context estimate R165 was suggestive. I register two lower-threshold core-negative interaction tests: Wnt activity at least 0.25 and AXL expression at least 3.5, both direction -1. These increase sample size while still testing whether the PTEN association is context-specific within a population where the four strongest markers are absent, reducing confounding by the dominant marker effects. If these interactions are imprecise or null, PTEN context-specific subgroup means should continue to be reported only as robustness evidence, not as accepted effect modification. Insufficient cell counts would be treated as design limitations, not as empirical nulls. Multiplicity remains substantial, so any acceptance should require both size and interval support, not a nominally favorable point estimate. All conclusions remain dataset-level associations and do not establish causality, single-gene mechanism, biological meaning of constructed signatures or markers, or generalizability beyond this dataset.",
