imate R74 = 0.139 [0.065, 0.213] is below the threshold point, and after validation and multiplicity it is better reported as not robustly associated. Insufficient-cell contrasts are design limitations, not empirical nulls.\n\nInteractions. No direct interaction has been accepted as meaningful effect modification. Many simple subgroup estimates for the four strong markers and PTEN are robust, but interaction contrasts generally have intervals that include zero and values below the practical threshold. Rejections against the stronger-context direction include PTEN high-AXL core-negative H231/R231 = -0.097 [-0.283, 0.089] and SMARCA4 high-MYC H132/R239 = -0.044 [-0.190, 0.103]. The most suggestive but still unresolved signals are PTEN attenuation in core-negative high-MYC cells, attenuation-signed H229/H232/R229 = 0.187 [0.031, 0.343], and the broader core-negative MYC threshold 5.0 interaction H236 = 0.173 [0.019, 0.327]. TP53-loss by high MYC H234 = 0.164 [0.034, 0.295] is also suggestive but imprecise. MSI-high slower-growth attenuation remains suggestive but not accepted, H225/R225 = -0.368 [-0.672, -0.064] against the stronger-context claim, with attenuation-signed interval 0.368 [0.064, 0.672], while the broader growth test H237 = 0.090 [-0.155, 0.335] is inconclusive. PTEN lower screen quality, fast growth, high-Wnt, stemness, hypoxia, and broader screen-quality interactions remain imprecise, for example R207, R216, and R217 have lower bounds below threshold.\n\nMost informative next analysis. I registered three focused discovery direct interactions to address the main unresolved PTEN question: whether PTEN-loss is genuinely attenuated in TP53-loss cells, SMARCA4-loss cells, or high mutation-burden cells. These are attenuation tests with direction +1; a positive signed interaction would mean the PTEN stronger-dependency association is smaller in the named context than in its complement. Acceptance should require a signed interval supporting attenuation and compatible with the 0.15-unit threshold. Null or imprecise results would support additive robustness of the accepted PTEN association rather than accepted effect modification. All conclusions remain dataset-specific associations from the supplied dataset and do not establish causality, single-gene knockout mechanism, biological pathway interpretation, constructed-assay meaning, or generalizability beyond this dataset."
