cation because lower bounds are below the threshold, multiple subgroup/interaction searches were performed, and confounding by lineage, screen quality, Cas9 activity, growth rate, library, and correlated molecular features remains. Independent validation capacity is exhausted, so these cannot be resolved in this run.\n\nThe most informative next analysis is not broad exploratory mining but a small confirmatory panel with pre-specified decision rules. The first priority is TP53 loss by MYC-high, ideally MYC >=5.5, using a positive interaction direction, a large eligible core context or adjusted model, safeguards for cell counts and screen quality, and an acceptance rule requiring an independent or adjusted lower confidence bound above 0.15. Secondary priorities are PTEN loss by MYC-high in core-negative or Avana contexts and CDKN2A loss in large homogeneous core-negative strata with multiplicity control. All future conclusions should remain explicitly dataset-specific unless replicated in independent data, and biological interpretation of constructed signatures, markers, or composite dependency endpoints should not be inferred from associations alone.",
